ocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What happened?\n\nI am attempting to cross-compile a CGO library, and thus have to set the toolchain for selected targets (through `CC` env variable).\r\n\r\nWhen setting env variables in a build override - despite the arch/os matching - the overridden value is not set when actually performing the build.\r\n\r\nI can see the build matching the override rule:\r\n```\r\n• overridden build details for linuxarm64        details={[-s -w] [] [-buildmode=c-shared] [] [] [CC=zig cc -target aarch64-linux]}\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, when running \r\n\r\n```\r\n$ goreleaser build --debug\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn the list of environment variables I do not see the overridden value:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[...] CGO_ENABLED=1 CC=zig cc GOOS=linux GOARCH=arm64 GOARM= GOMIPS= GOMIPS64= GOAMD64=\r\n```\r\n\r\n`CC` in particular is supposed to appear twice, with the default value, plus the overridden one as `CC=zig cc -target aarch64-linux`.\n\n### How can we reproduce this?\n\nThe `.goreleaser.yml` where I found the issue:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/borgoat/farmfa/blob/ffi/.goreleaser.yml#L13-L42\n\n### goreleaser version\n\n```bash\ngoreleaser version dev\r\ngoos: linux\r\ngoarch: amd64\r\nmodule version: v1.10.1, checksum: h1:NXCiqc4DJAG0y+iXDZKQew+0logeuZhYrCn4KZOrF0o=\r\n\r\nhttps://goreleaser.com\n```\n\n\n### GoReleaser Check\n\n- [X] goreleaser check shows no errors\n\n### Search\n\n- [X] I did search for other open and closed issues before opening this.\n\n### Code of Conduct\n\n- [X] I agree to follow this project's Code of Conduct\n\n### Additional context\n\nThis is related to:\r\n\r\n* #3201 \r\n* #3119 ","closed_by":{"login":"caarlos0","id":245435,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NTQzNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245435?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caarlos0","html_url":"https://github.com/caarlos0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caarlos0/followers","following_url":"https:/